WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.751 --> 00:00:01.960
-  Okay, here we go.

00:00:04.922 --> 00:00:06.840
Switch over to the night camera.

00:00:06.924 --> 00:00:09.468
- We're using these
incredible cameras,

00:00:09.551 --> 00:00:12.262
gives us the ability to see
all this action at night.

00:00:12.888 --> 00:00:15.682
We're seeing an almost
daylight image.

00:00:15.766 --> 00:00:18.227
(elephant trumpeting)

00:00:22.022 --> 00:00:24.608
- It's amazing to film stuff
that's never been seen.

00:00:24.691 --> 00:00:26.193
Scientists don't even know
what happens.

00:00:26.652 --> 00:00:28.820
- These two male cheetahs
start hunting at nighttime,

00:00:28.904 --> 00:00:30.489
which is
unseen behavior.

00:00:30.572 --> 00:00:32.324
One of them's
starting to run in.

00:00:32.407 --> 00:00:34.076
The amount of nights
we've been out here...

00:00:35.285 --> 00:00:37.579
I can't believe we actually
got that shot finally.

00:00:37.663 --> 00:00:39.206
It's brilliant.

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:40.499
(growling)

00:00:40.582 --> 00:00:42.459
- We wanted to film the softer side.

00:00:42.543 --> 00:00:43.794
- Oh, wow.

00:00:43.877 --> 00:00:45.462
- Not many people know that
they live in

00:00:45.546 --> 00:00:47.464
these really lovely
family groups.

00:00:47.548 --> 00:00:50.467
We're hoping that we can
show a world that no one's seen before.

00:00:50.551 --> 00:00:53.053
- We're only beginning
to understand

00:00:53.136 --> 00:00:55.639
the strange things
that take place at night.

00:00:57.057 --> 00:01:00.018
- It's all very well doing
this sort of thing in daylight.

00:01:00.102 --> 00:01:02.020
We're trying to
take it on at night.

00:01:02.104 --> 00:01:04.565
That adds layers
and layers of problems.

00:01:04.648 --> 00:01:07.693
You obviously look down,
you can't see what's happening.

00:01:07.776 --> 00:01:10.863
- Uh, yeah, that looks amazing.
I can just...

00:01:10.946 --> 00:01:13.240
- Yeah, it's great. Wow.

00:01:14.616 --> 00:01:18.078
- This is definitely one of
the hardest shoots I've been on.

00:01:18.161 --> 00:01:19.621
It's about minus 30
out here.

00:01:21.582 --> 00:01:23.917
- Having to constantly look out
for predators like bears,

00:01:24.001 --> 00:01:24.960
it's a big worry.

00:01:25.043 --> 00:01:28.005
Wow. You can actually
see teeth marks

00:01:28.088 --> 00:01:29.965
and claw marks where
the bear's been.

00:01:33.093 --> 00:01:35.679
- Key here to filming is when they move,
you gotta stick with them,

00:01:35.762 --> 00:01:38.765
but in a way where you're not interfering,
especially if they're hunting.

00:01:44.438 --> 00:01:46.648
- I'm really, really happy
to have seen that.

00:01:46.732 --> 00:01:47.983
Oh, that's so cool.

00:01:48.984 --> 00:01:51.778
- Turns us humans
into nocturnal animals.

00:01:53.030 --> 00:01:55.324
- Being able to sit out here
with them in the dark

00:01:55.407 --> 00:01:58.243
is pretty incredible to see
a new life of an animal.

00:01:59.369 --> 00:02:02.581
- We can reveal how magic
the night world really is.

00:02:02.664 --> 00:02:04.499
(trumpeting)

00:02:11.131 --> 00:02:12.925
- That's really amazing to see.

00:02:13.008 --> 00:02:15.010
(lion growling)

